rav1d 1.1.0 — declare the nine dav1d_* shims Maple calls as `extern "C-unwind"`.

Maple issue #3517. rav1d's decoder panics on some corrupt AV1 streams (e.g.
`Option::unwrap()` at src/decode.rs:4997 for a truncated OBU). Its Rust-ABI
entry points are `pub(crate)`, so raw-core has to call the `pub unsafe extern
"C" fn dav1d_*` shims in src/lib.rs — and since Rust 1.81 a panic that reaches
a plain `extern "C"` frame aborts the process instead of unwinding. That kills
the whole API FFI child (and the test binary) before raw-ffi's `catch_panic_rc`
barrier can turn it into an error.

`extern "C-unwind"` keeps the identical C calling convention and symbol names —
C callers of the staticlib are unaffected — while permitting a Rust panic to
unwind back out through the shim, where raw-core's `catch_unwind` in
`avif_decode.rs` maps it to a decode error.

Only the nine shims raw-core actually calls are changed; the rest of the C API
is left alone so the delta stays minimal and reviewable.

Apply from src/raw-pipeline/third_party/rav1d:
    patch -p1 < ../../patches/rav1d-1.1.0-c-unwind.patch

